    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Admissions-Counselor_JR102057": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102057 Admissions Counselor (Open) Department: Admissions, Asst. Dir./Admissions | PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 08-03-2026 Close Date: $50,000 Job Description: Frostburg State University (FSU), Office of Admissions seeks applications for a full-time, exempt Admissions Counselor position. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience.  Position includes the robust University System of Maryland benefits package, which is comprised of annual, personal, and sick leave, holidays, tuition remission, health, dental, vision, and life insurance, and retirement plans. Responsibilities: Under the direction of an Assistant Director of Admissions, the Admissions Counselor is responsible for providing information regarding admissions standards and requirements for prospective students. Work directly with prospective students through the admissions, financial aid, scholarship, and application process. Implement recruitment activities such as campus trips, presentations, Saturday visits, virtual events, resource tables, application workshops, and designated area projects. Frequent travel to high schools and two-year colleges with some overnight travel required. Other duties as needed to assist with student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree with one to three years of related experience. The successful candidate will have excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills with a proven ability to interact effectively and promote a culturally diverse prospective student population.  Valid non-commercial driver’s license and a desire to travel required.  Ability to work nights and weekends as needed to assist with student enrollment.  Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of Customer Relationship Management system (CRM). About the University: A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. More than 4,000 students enroll yearly. About the Area: FSU is located on a scenic 260-acre campus in the mountains of Western Maryland, a region rich in history, quaint shopping areas and eclectic cafes and food choices. The Western Maryland region is considered a four-season outdoor hub of recreational experiences offering activities such as hiking, mountain biking, water sports, snow skiing/boarding, golfing, climbing, etc. Frostburg offers a family-friendly college town feel with easy access to major cities like Pittsburgh, Washington, DC, and Baltimore. If you are looking for insightful colleagues, energetic students, and a great place to work and call home in a region with unlimited adventure seeking opportunities, FSU is for you! To Apply: If you wish to apply, please visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers Along with your application, please provide the following: 1) resume; 2) a cover letter specifically addressing the requirements in this advertisement; 3) names and contact information for three professional references. For assurance of full consideration, please submit materials by August 17, 2026.  This position is open until filled. Additional Job Information: Admissions Counselor FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Assistant-Director-of-Operations_JR102055": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102055 Assistant Director of Operations (Open) Department: Director of Lane University Center and Event Services | PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 07-27-2026 Close Date: $60,000 - $65,000 Job Description: Assistant Director of Operations Frostburg State University, Department of Student Engagement , seeks applications for a full-time, exempt Assistant Director of Operations position in the Lane University Center & Event Services to begin Fall 2026. Salary commensurate with qualifications and includes University System of Maryland benefits package. The Lane University Center serves as a dynamic gathering place where students connect, lead, learn, and build community. Through a vibrant environment, the Lane University Center & Event Services team supports student success by fostering meaningful involvement opportunities, campus experiences, and creating spaces that promote belonging and engagement. Annually, the department hosts more than 6,000 meetings and events. The successful candidate will join a collaborative team within the Office of Student Engagement, working alongside campus partners to enhance the overall student experience. Responsibilities : Reporting to the Director of the Lane University Center & Event Services, the Assistant Director of Operations assists in the overall management, operation, and production of the Lane University Center technical services. This position recruits, trains, supervises, and develops the student Technical Services Crew while overseeing the technical planning, production, and operational support of events serving students, faculty, staff, and external clients. The Assistant Director collaborates with campus partners to deliver exceptional event experiences, maintain and enhance facility technologies and systems, support risk management and operational initiatives, and contribute to the Lane Center's mission of enhancing student engagement, building community, and enriching the overall Frostburg State University experience. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and one year of experience with facility operations in a student union/university center, technical direction, or related field. Demonstrated experience with event production including audio, lighting, and video. Demonstrated experience dealing with clients, providing detailed customer service, and meeting production deadlines is required. Valid non-commercial driver’s license. Must be available to work nights and weekends. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in management, technical theater, or a related field. More than three years of experience with student union operations, technical theater, technical direction, electronic media/film, events, or related field. Experience working with and supervising students in a college environment. Experience with event scheduling software (EMS) and large scale, concert lighting/sound system operation. Other: Any combination of training and experience substantially equivalent to graduation from an accredited college or university with a bachelor’s degree in a related field and progressively responsible related work experience may be considered. About the University: A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. Approximately 4,000 students enroll yearly. About the Area: FSU is located on a scenic 260-acre campus in the gorgeous mountains of Western Maryland. Affectionately referred to as Mountain Maryland, our region is the outdoor enthusiasts’ paradise, offering a combined 600 miles of biking and hiking trails, numerous lakes, rivers, streams, and waterfalls and 170,000 acres of public land, including 12 state parks, three state forests and one national park. With four seasons of outdoor recreation, including hunting, fishing, hiking, skiing & snowboarding, biking, rock climbing, world-class whitewater rafting, kayaking, recreational boating and off-road vehicle trails, Mountain Maryland offers a great quality of life and the ideal opportunity to craft your own work/life balance. With a reputation for safe communities, excellent schools and competitive wages, Mountain Maryland is a great place to raise a family and create a community of like-minded, outdoor adventure seeking, friends and colleagues.  Frostburg offers a family-friendly college town feel with easy access to major cities like Pittsburgh, Washington, DC, and Baltimore. If you are looking for a great place to live, work, and play in a beautiful mountain region with access to unlimited outdoor recreation adventure, FSU is for you! To Apply: Please visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers Along with your application, please provide the following: 1) resume; 2) a cover letter specifically addressing the requirements in this advertisement; and 3) contact information for three professional references. For full consideration, please apply by August 10, 2026 Additional Job Information: Assistant Director FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
