    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Assistant-Director-of-Residence-Life-for-Residential-Education_JR102054": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Residence Life for Residential Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR102054 Assistant Director of Residence Life for Residential Education (Open) Department: Residence Life, Director, RLO | PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 07-27-2026 Close Date: $58,000 - $61,000 Job Description: Assistant Director of Residence Life for Residential Education Frostburg State University, Residence Life Office , invites applications for the Assistant Director of Residence Life for Residential Education within the Division of Student Affairs. The Division of Student Affairs at Frostburg State University is characterized by a commitment to the development of the whole student in an engaged learning community. This full-time, exempt position provides leadership for on-campus Residential Education program at FSU. Salary commensurate with experience and includes University System of Maryland benefits package. Responsibilities: Reporting to the Director of Residence Life, the Assistant Director will provide leadership and direction for the residential education aspects of the housing program.  Responsibilities include serving as the supervisor of Residential Leadership professional and para-professional staff, supervision of the Residential Student Mailroom Clerk and student workers. Responsible for recruiting, selecting, supervising and evaluating professional Residential Leadership professional and para-professional staff. Participation in the residential conduct process. Manage the residential leadership program, oversea programming, supplies, and curriculum. Participate in on-call duty rotation. Engage with parents and students. Participate in residence life processes, including, but not limited to openings, closings, and staff recruitment. Responsible for the Residential Leadership Programs and space, and responsible for RLO social media. Other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in higher education administration, student affairs, college student personnel administration, or related field. Two to four years post Bachelor’s experience in Residence Life or Higher Education. Experience with student programming. Excellent oral and written communications skills, computer literacy and experience with databases, data analysis and housing management software. Demonstrated ability to set priorities and accomplish tasks effectively. Demonstrated knowledge of and experience in higher education development theory, risk management and legal issues. Ability to relate effectively and positively with students, parents, faculty and staff. Preferred Qualifications: Four or more years of experience with Residential Leadership programs in residence life, higher education or similar settings. Supervision experience. Other: Any combination of training and experience substantially equivalent to graduation from an accredited college or university with a master’s degree in a related field and progressively responsible related work experience may be considered. About the University: A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. Approximately 4,000 students enroll yearly. About the Area: FSU is located on a scenic 260-acre campus in the gorgeous mountains of Western Maryland. Affectionately referred to as Mountain Maryland, our region is the outdoor enthusiasts’ paradise, offering a combined 600 miles of biking and hiking trails, numerous lakes, rivers, streams, and waterfalls and 170,000 acres of public land, including 12 state parks, three state forests and one national park. With four seasons of outdoor recreation, including hunting, fishing, hiking, skiing & snowboarding, biking, rock climbing, world-class whitewater rafting, kayaking, recreational boating and off-road vehicle trails, Mountain Maryland offers a great quality of life and the ideal opportunity to craft your own work/life balance. With a reputation for safe communities, excellent schools and competitive wages, Mountain Maryland is a great place to raise a family and create a community of like-minded, outdoor adventure seeking, friends and colleagues.  Frostburg offers a family-friendly college town feel with easy access to major cities like Pittsburgh, Washington, DC, and Baltimore. If you are looking for a great place to live, work, and play in a beautiful mountain region with access to unlimited outdoor recreation adventure, FSU is for you! To Apply: Please visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers Along with your application, please provide the following: 1) resume; 2) a cover letter specifically addressing the requirements in this advertisement; and 3) contact information for three professional references. For full consideration, please apply by August 10, 2026 Position is open until filled. Additional Job Information: Assistant Director FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
