    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Clinical-Placement-Coordinator_JR101993": {
      "title": "Clinical Placement Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR101993 Clinical Placement Coordinator (Open) Department: Nursing, Associate Professor | PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 07-08-2026 Close Date: $60,000 - $66,000 Job Description: Clinical Placement Coordinator The Department of Nursing at Frostburg State University invites applications for a full-time Clinical Placement Coordinator. This position plays a critical role in supporting student success by coordinating clinical placements for nursing students across undergraduate and graduate programs. Some travel may be required. About the Department The Department of Nursing is one of Frostburg State University's largest academic departments, offering a range of undergraduate and graduate nursing programs in both on-campus and online formats. The department is supported by a dedicated team of faculty and staff committed to excellence in nursing education and student achievement. Position Summary The Clinical Placement Coordinator is responsible for facilitating and managing clinical placements for nursing students. This position serves as the primary liaison between students, healthcare organizations, and the university to ensure students secure appropriate clinical experiences that meet program and course requirements. Primary Responsibilities Coordinate clinical placements for undergraduate and graduate nursing students. Assist students in identifying and securing clinical sites that align with course and program requirements. Serve as the primary point of contact between students and clinical agencies. Establish and maintain positive relationships with healthcare organizations and clinical partners. Coordinate with clinical agencies and the University's legal department to develop and execute new affiliation agreements. Ensure students understand and complete all requirements established by clinical organizations. Monitor placement progress and maintain accurate records of clinical placements and agreements. Communicate regularly with nursing faculty and department leadership regarding placement status and emerging needs. Collaborate with faculty and staff to address and resolve clinical placement challenges. Support ongoing efforts to expand and strengthen clinical partnership opportunities. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree or higher Strong organizational, communication, and relationship-building skills. Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines simultaneously. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and database management systems. Preferred Qualifications Two or more years of work experience in a professional setting. Experience working with healthcare organizations, higher education, clinical education, or student support services preferred. Why Join Frostburg State University? This position offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the educational experiences of future nurses while working within a collaborative and student-centered academic environment. Interested candidates are encouraged to apply and become part of a dynamic nursing department dedicated to preparing the next generation of nursing professionals. To Apply: Please visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers Along with your application, please provide the following: 1) resume; 2) a cover letter specifically addressing the requirements in this advertisement; and 3) contact information for three professional references. For consideration, please apply by July 22, 2026 This position is open until filled. Additional Job Information: Coordinator FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Lecturer-of-Nursing---Nurse-Practitioner-Concentrations_JR101989": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Nursing - Nurse Practitioner Concentrations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR101989 Lecturer of Nursing - Nurse Practitioner Concentrations (Open) Department: Nursing, Associate Professor | PM Position Type: Non-Regular Fixed Term (Fixed Term) Open Date: 07-07-2026 Close Date: $80,000 Job Description: FTNTT Lecturer of Nursing - Nurse Practitioner Concentrations Frostburg State University seeks qualified applicants for a full-time non-tenure track (FTNTT) Lecturer in our Department of Nursing. This position is to serve as faculty member in the new Post-Masters Nurse Practitioner Certificate programs that are anticipated to begin Fall 2027. This is a full-time, 10-month contractual faculty position with teaching, service, and professional development responsibilities, that will begin Fall 2026. Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications; University System of Maryland benefits package included. The Department of Nursing at FSU provides a variety of undergraduate and graduate nursing programs and pathways including a new online LPN to BSN, a new on-campus BSN program, an online RN to BSN, and four graduate nursing concentrations. This faculty position is to teach primarily within the undergraduate on-campus and online programs. The Department of Nursing is a dynamic, fast-paced environment that thrives on the strengths of each team member. We are looking for individuals that enjoy working in a collaborative team environment and are experienced in developing innovative and creative teaching strategies focused on student success. Successful candidates will have a strong commitment to promoting diversity and have respect for our diverse student population. Responsibilities: Teach 24 credits each academic year in the online and hybrid format at the graduate level. Advise graduate students. Design curriculum and design and coordinate curriculum in area of specialty/expertise.  Devote efforts to scholarly activities and professional development.  Provide service activities to the department, college, university, community, and/or profession.  Other academic duties as assigned. Maintaining active practice is required to teach graduate level clinical courses. This is a hybrid position requiring on-campus time each month for meetings, and some days each semester for graduate student laboratory requirements. Minimum Qualifications: Earned graduate degree in family nurse practitioner and/or psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner from a regionally accredited university. Unrestricted APRN license or eligible for licensure in Maryland. We are seeking applicants with recent clinical nursing practice and/or considerable professional development related to clinical nursing practice. The successful candidate will display evidence of leadership skills and excellent interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications : Earned or in progress doctoral degree in nursing or related field. Dual certification in family and psychiatric nurse practitioner. About the University:  A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts, and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. More than 4,000 students enroll yearly. About the Area:  FSU is located on a scenic 260-acre campus in the mountains of Western Maryland, a region rich in history, quaint shopping areas and eclectic cafes and food choices. The Western Maryland region is considered a four-season outdoor hub of recreational experiences offering activities such as hiking, mountain biking, water sports, snowboarding, skiing, golfing, climbing, etc. Frostburg offers a family-friendly college town feel with easy access to major cities like Pittsburgh, Washington, and Baltimore. If you are looking for insightful colleagues, energetic students, and a great place to work and call home in a region with unlimited adventure seeking opportunities, FSU is for you! To Apply: Please visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers Along with your application, please provide the following: 1) curriculum vitae; 2) a cover letter specifically addressing the requirements in this advertisement; 3) a brief statement on your teaching philosophy; 4) a brief statement outlining your commitment to inclusion and diversity; 5) contact information for three professional references; and 6) unofficial transcripts of your graduate work. Please note: the contributions to diversity, equity and inclusion statement should describe your past experience, activities, and future plans to advance diversity, equity and inclusion, in alignment with FSU’s mission to reflect the diversity of our campus and to meet the educational needs and interests of our diverse population. Some faculty candidates may not have substantial past activities. If that is the case, we recommend focusing on future plans in your statement. For assurance of full consideration, please submit materials by August 4 , 2026 . This position is open until filled. Additional Job Information: Lecturer FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Manager-of-Specifications_JR101871": {
      "title": "Manager of Specifications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR101871 Manager of Specifications (Open) Department: Physical Plant, Director of Physical Plant | PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 06-29-2026 Close Date: $87,000 Job Description: Manager of Specifications Frostburg State University (FSU) seeks applications for an exempt full-time Manager of Specifications. Position includes the University of Maryland benefits package which includes annual leave, holidays, personal, and sick leave; tuition remission; excellent health and life insurance, and retirement plans. Responsibilities: Develops, plans, and bid documents for the University’s facility/auxiliary and capital construction projects. The Manager of Specifications will be responsible for managing all aspects of new construction and renovation projects, preparing budget estimates and reports, preparing project and contract documents, overseeing outside design professionals, and preparation of construction documents. This position will also manage the project team throughout both the design and construction to include monitoring the contractor’s progress, quality of work, materials compliance, coordinating engineering problem areas with contractors, reviewing engineering drawings for constructability and design, and preparing various construction related permitting documents. Position is required to manage and coordinate projects from conception to completion. Position reports to the Assistant Director of Facilities for Planning and Construction. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science in architecture or civil, electrical, or mechanical engineering, or related field. Must be proficient and current in AutoCAD for plan preparations. Preferred Qualifications: Five years of relevant work experience. Experience with design, creating specifications, COMAR, OSHA, and commercial construction and construction management. About the University: A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. More than 4,000 students enroll yearly. About the Area: FSU is located on a scenic 260-acre campus in the mountains of Western Maryland, a region rich in history, quaint shopping areas and eclectic cafes and food choices. The Western Maryland region is considered to be a four-season outdoor mecca of recreational experiences offering activities such as; hiking, mountain biking, water sports, snow skiing/boarding, golfing, climbing, etc.  Frostburg offers a family-friendly college town feel with easy access to major cities like Pittsburgh, Washington, DC, and Baltimore. If you are looking for insightful colleagues, energetic students, and a great place to work and call home in a region with unlimited adventure seeking opportunities, FSU is for you! If you wish to apply, please visit: https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers For assurance of full consideration, please submit materials by July 13, 2026. Position open until filled. Additional Job Information: Construction Projects Coordinator FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Head-of-Technical-Services_JR101968": {
      "title": "Head of Technical Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR101968 Head of Technical Services (Open) Department: Library, Director of Library | PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 06-29-2026 Close Date: $75,000 - $81,000 Job Description: Head of Technical Services Frostburg State University, Lewis J. Ort Library , seeks applications for a full-time, faculty level position as the Head of Technical Services. Salary commensurate with experience; University System of Maryland benefits package included. Frostburg State University seeks a dynamic, forward-thinking, collaborative individual with demonstrated experience and potential to provide innovative strategies for supporting student learning and scholarly research while promoting a culture of excellent service to library users. Responsibilities: Directs all functions of the Library’s Technical Services Unit, including providing strategic direction and supervising staff fulfilling daily operations in acquisitions, serials, cataloging/metadata, and electronic resources management. Develops, implements and evaluates policies and procedures pertaining to the acquisition and access; cataloging and classification; and deselection and withdrawal of library materials. Oversees management of the library materials budget in consultation with the Director of Library Services. Manages critical components of the electronic resources lifecycle. Performs original and copy cataloging and establishes local descriptive metadata standards. Oversees the maintenance and integrity of the library's online bibliographic and associated records in the USMAI Library Consortium shared integrated library system. Coordinates the library’s shared print initiatives. Collects, analyzes, and reports statistics to inform evidence-based collection development decisions. Serves as a liaison to assigned academic departments. Represents the library on relevant University and system-wide committees. Engages in professional scholarship and service activities in fulfillment of University System of Maryland and Frostburg State University promotion standards and procedures. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s in Library Science degree from an American Library Association (ALA) accredited program. Minimum of three years of successful, progressively responsible professional experience in technical services that includes administrative or supervisory experience. Demonstrated experience with integrated library systems, discovery systems, and bibliographic utilities. The ability to catalog a broad range of subjects and formats. Working knowledge or experience with RDA and MARC21 formats, Library of Congress Classification and Subject Headings, OCLC, and authority control procedures. Working knowledge of issues related to electronic resource management. Strong analytical, problem solving, and organizational skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with technical services workflows in an Ex Libris Alma ILS environment. Experience with collection development theory and practices in an academic library. Experience with budget management. Experience with descriptive metadata for digitized and born-digital content. Working knowledge of library analytic tools and usage data platforms. Demonstrated understanding of current trends in technical services. Record of scholarship and professional achievement appropriate for appointment in faculty rank. About the University: A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. Approximately 4,000 students enroll yearly. About the Area: FSU is located on a scenic 260-acre campus in the gorgeous mountains of Western Maryland. Affectionately referred to as Mountain Maryland, our region is the outdoor enthusiasts’ paradise, offering a combined 600 miles of biking and hiking trails, numerous lakes, rivers, streams, and waterfalls and 170,000 acres of public land, including 12 state parks, three state forests and one national park. With four seasons of outdoor recreation, including hunting, fishing, hiking, skiing & snowboarding, biking, rock climbing, world-class whitewater rafting, kayaking, recreational boating and off-road vehicle trails, Mountain Maryland offers a great quality of life and the ideal opportunity to craft your own work/life balance. With a reputation for safe communities, excellent schools and competitive wages, Mountain Maryland is a great place to raise a family and create a community of like-minded, outdoor adventure seeking, friends and colleagues.  Frostburg offers a family-friendly college town feel with easy access to major cities like Pittsburgh, Washington, DC, and Baltimore. If you are looking for a great place to live, work, and play in a beautiful mountain region with access to unlimited outdoor recreation adventure, FSU is for you! To Apply: Please visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers . Along with your application, please provide the following: 1) resume; 2) a cover letter specifically addressing the requirements in this advertisement; and 3) contact information for three professional references. For full assurance of consideration please apply by July 13, 2026. This position is open until filled. Additional Job Information: Library Supervisor FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Carpenter_JR101964": {
      "title": "Carpenter",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR101964 Carpenter (Open) Department: Physical Plant, Assistant Director of Facilities | PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 06-26-2026 Close Date: $23.08/hour Job Description: Carpenter Frostburg State University, Physical Plant Department, seeks applications for a full-time, non-exempt Carpenter position. Hourly rate $23.08; Position includes the robust University System of Maryland benefits package, which is comprised of annual, personal, and sick leave, holidays, tuition remission, health, dental, vision, and life insurance, and retirement plans. Responsibilities : Under general supervision, performs rough and finish carpentry work at the journeyman level. Constructs, installs, repairs, and maintains structures and fixtures using wood and wood-like materials (including plastics and fiberglass). Builds concrete forms, scaffolds, frameworks, platforms, and general supports in accordance with blueprints, drawings, specifications, and oral or written instructions. Utilizes comprehensive knowledge of carpentry and joinery methods and techniques, as well as the properties and characteristics of wood and related materials. Measures, cuts, shapes, and installs materials with precision, using and maintaining hand and power tools and equipment associated with the carpentry trade. Reads and interprets blueprints, drawings, and specifications to complete assigned projects. Applies basic mathematics, including area, volume, weights, fractions, percentages, ratios, and proportions, in daily work activities. Adheres to OSHA regulations and established safety procedures at all times. Prepares basic work summaries or reports as needed and communicates effectively with supervisors and team members. Performs work in, on, around, over, and under fixed equipment and machinery, including working from ladders and scaffolding. Safely handles tools, equipment, and materials, including lifting or exerting force up to 70 lbs., and may operate equipment requiring the coordination of multiple controls. Works in potentially hazardous or irritating environments, confined spaces, and adverse weather or temperature conditions while properly using required personal protective equipment (PPE). Performs other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Four years of progressively responsible experience in the carpentry trade.  Successful completion of a pre-employment physical examination. Valid non-commercial driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in commercial building. Other: Except for qualifications established by law, additional related experience and formal education in which one has gained the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for full performance of the work of the job class may be substituted for the education or experience requirement on a year-for-year basis with 30 college credits being equivalent to one year of experience. About the University: A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. More than 4,000 students enroll yearly. To apply, visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers For assurance of full consideration, please submit materials by July 10, 2026. This position is open until filled. Additional Job Information: FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Principal-Faculty---Physician-Assistant-Program_JR101713": {
      "title": "Principal Faculty - Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Posting: JR101713 Principal Faculty - Physician Assistant Program (Open) Department: Physician Assistant Medicine, Director, PA Program | PM Position Type: Regular Open Date: 04-15-2026 Close Date: $108,000 - $112,000 Job Description: Principal Faculty Physician Assistant Program Frostburg State University seeks qualified applicants for a Principal Faculty member for our fully accredited Physician Assistant (PA) program in Hagerstown, Maryland. This is a 12-month contract (annual renewal) position as a full-time, tenure-track faculty member with the rank of Assistant Professor and associated teaching responsibility. Salary is commensurate with education, experience, and qualifications and benefits package includes University System of Maryland (USM) health care benefits, professional development funds, and tuition remission. The PA Program is in the Department of Physician Assistant Medicine (DPAM) and the College of Education, Behavioral and Health Professions (CEBHP). Given the mission of the program and institution, we encourage prospective candidates with the following experience to apply: demonstrated commitment to advancing health and wellness, research, systems-innovation, or practice experience for/with underserved areas/populations, leadership (formal or informal) related to health equity, with welcomed diversity of perspective and approaches, and modeled respect for diverse populations and an advocate to the PA profession or  health care professions team, reflective of individuals we serve in the community, educate in the program, and work alongside as team members. To learn more, visit our Department and the PA Program: online: https://www.frostburg.edu/programs/graduate-physician-assistant/welcome.php Responsibilities and Duties : Contribute meaningfully as a faculty role model providing graduate-level education in the PA program through Teaching and related roles. Participate in Service activities that support the mission of the program, department, and institution, including committees, professional organization involvement or leadership. Engage in ongoing Professional Development and scholarly works to maintain and/or advance personal/career growth, the profession, program and/or institution, research knowledge, evidence-based practice, and interprofessional education. Meet and maintain the requirements of a faculty member*, described in the FSU Faculty Handbook and located on the institution’s website. In the PA program, Principal Faculty maintain responsibility for the following (ARC-PA Standards, 6th edition, Sept 2025) (A2.05): developing, reviewing, and revising as necessary the program’s mission statement, goals, and competencies selecting applicants for admission to the PA program providing student instruction evaluating student performance academic counseling of students assuring the availability of remedial instruction designing, implementing, coordinating, and evaluating the curriculum evaluating the program *Note: Principal faculty hold academic appointments and privileges comparable to other faculty with similar academic responsibilities within the institution (A2.04). Minimum Qualifications: Physician Assistant/Associate Master’s degree from an accredited PA program, or its equivalence if, including terminal degree at the time of completion. Current license, unencumbered Current board certification - NCCPA certified or emeritus Physician Degree from an accredited medical school Current license, unencumbered, as an osteopathic or allopathic physician Current or previously board-certified Other Healthcare Professionals Terminal degree from a health professions-related program (Master’s level or Doctoral degree) Current license, unencumbered Current board certification Non-Clinical Professionals Terminal degree from a related field to health professions education, graduate medical education, or related focus. Doctoral degree (e.g., PhD, EdD) Other requirements: Prior teaching experience in higher education or other relevant experience that demonstrates an ability to provide complex or rigorous instruction with associated assessment measures, even if occurring in non-traditional settings Excellent interpersonal communication skills – oral and written. Demonstrated history of leadership, advocacy, and administrator-related effectiveness. General knowledge and understanding of the PA profession and associated practice. Collaboration and appreciation for team-based approaches are evident in prior practice, work, or research activities. Preferred Qualifications: Two or more years of relevant experience (clinical or non-clinical) working in/with underserved areas/populations, rural areas, or other related experiences supporting or linking to the program’s and/or institution’s mission; Teaching in higher education and/or administrative experience in academia, PA education, or a related field; Knowledge of PA program administration, organization, operations, curriculum, evaluation, and accreditation. Professional interest in and consistent works related to research or scholarly activities that relate to the faculty role, the program’s mission, or the betterment of population. Participation/leadership in local, state, regional, or professional national organizations. About the University:  A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts, and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. More than 4,000 students enroll yearly. About the Area:  USMH is in downtown Hagerstown a growing area with the opening of a new baseball stadium, updates to the Maryland Theatre, and other economic development initiatives. Hagerstown and Washington County offers easy access to major cities like Pittsburgh, Washington, DC, and Baltimore, historic local small towns, wineries, brew pubs, artisan shops, and 5 national parks. If you are ready to work as part of a small team, excited to grow, and committed to supporting learning, USMH is a great environment for you.  To Apply: Visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers .  Along with your application, please provide the following: 1) curriculum vitae; 2) a cover letter specifically addressing the requirements in this advertisement; 3) statement on teaching philosophy; 4) contact information for three professional references; and 5) unofficial transcripts of your graduate work.  For assurance of full consideration, please submit materials by April 29 , 2026. This position is open until filled. FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU Additional Job Information: Assistant Professor FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
    },
    "https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Frostburg-State-University/Adjunct-Lecturers---Music-Private-Instruction_JR100844-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer Pool:  Music Private Instruction",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Posting: JR100844 Adjunct Lecturer Pool: Music Private Instruction (Evergreen) (Open) Department: Music, Theatre, and Dance, Associate Professor | JM Position Type: Non-Regular Fixed Term (Fixed Term) Open Date: 04-14-2026 Close Date: $750 - $2,000 per course Job Description: Adjunct Lecturers:  Music Private Instruction Frostburg State University, Department of Music , seeks part-time Adjunct Lecturers to teach private instruction in the following areas: Flute Oboe Horn Trumpet Low Brass (trombone/euphonium/tuba) Upper Strings (violin/viola) Guitar Piano Organ Voice Direct position inquiries to Dr. Brent Weber, Chair of the Department of Music, at 301-687-4116 or bmweber@frostburg.edu Responsibilities: Provide private instruction to undergraduate music majors and minors. The opportunity to teach other music related courses may be available on an as-needed basis. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in music or a related area required. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience at the collegiate level preferred. About the University: A member institution of the University System of Maryland, Frostburg State University is a public, comprehensive, largely residential regional university offering programs in the sciences, education, business, the arts and humanities at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. FSU prides itself on being a dynamic, learning-centered institution that emphasizes teaching with opportunities for professional development and research. More than 4,000 students enroll yearly. About the Area: FSU is located on a scenic 260-acre campus in the mountains of Western Maryland, a region rich in history, quaint shopping areas and eclectic cafes and food choices. The Western Maryland region is considered a four-season outdoor hub of recreational experiences offering activities such as hiking, mountain biking, water sports, snow skiing/boarding, golfing, climbing, etc. Frostburg offers a family-friendly college town feel with easy access to major cities like Pittsburgh, Washington, DC, and Baltimore. If you are looking for insightful colleagues, energetic students, and a great place to work and call home in a region with unlimited adventure seeking opportunities, FSU is for you! To Apply: Please visit https://marylandconnect.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FSU_Careers Along with your application, please provide the following: 1) Curriculum Vitae; 2) a letter of interest; 3) list of three professional references, 4) unofficial graduate transcripts, and 5) link to recent performances. Position availability depends on the area in need at a given time FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disabilities will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU Additional Job Information: Adjunct Faculty I FSU is proud to be a diverse and inclusive multicultural university. Frostburg State University welcomes and encourages women, veterans and minorities to apply and seeks to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.  FSU is an  Equal Opportunity Employer .  Appropriate auxiliary aids and services for qualified individuals with disability will be provided upon request.  Please notify us in advance.  WWW.FROSTBURG.EDU"
